**Semantic search (SSE decoding)**  
SSE wire-format parsing lives in two in-repo places:

1. **TypeScript SDK** — `createSseClient` in 12 generated copies of `packages/sdk/generated/*/core/serverSentEvents.gen.ts`. It reads `response.body` via `TextDecoderStream`, splits on `\n\n`, and parses `data:` / `event:` / `id:` / `retry:` lines. Wired from each service’s `client.gen.ts` via `makeSseFn`. No current product callers of `client.sse.*`.

2. **Rust Anthropic client** — `Client::post_stream` in `crates/anthropic/src/client/mod.rs`. Line-oriented parse of `data: ` prefixes from the HTTP body; called from `Chat::create_stream`. JSON is then deserialized as `StreamEvent`.

Related but not in-repo: `eventsource-stream` inside `async-openai` / `rig-core`. Product chat streaming uses WebSocket JSON (`connection_gateway`), not HTTP SSE. There is no `SseDecoder` type.

